<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kharg Island</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kharg Island is a small island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Persian Gulf</a> off the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, north-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bushehr">Bushehr</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> built a fort and trading post there in the 1750s, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mir-muhanna">Mir Muhanna</a>, lord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bandar-rig">Bandar Rig</a>, seized in the 1760s. Since the 1960s it has been Iran's main crude-oil export terminal, and it was repeatedly bombed in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran-iraq-war">Iran–Iraq War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kharg-island.jpg" alt="Kharg Island" width="320" height="485" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johnson Space Center · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ISS005-E-11900_lrg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
